# `On unmatch` (and the Destructor command under it) dereferences the
# current match without checking that there is one. The top level of the
# boot program, which is also how every file in test/ runs, has none.
# See FINDINGS.md, E2.
#
# Expected: an error, or the body running at exit.
# Observed: the process dies with SIGSEGV (exit status 139).

On unmatch { puts "cleaning up" }
Exit! 0
